course: dictionary
lesson: 11138
title: Width
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Width is how wide something is. It is the distance from one side to the other, measured across, not along. Think of a doorway: the width is the gap between the two door frames.
explain: Width is a noun, so you can say «the width of the road» or «the width of a bed». In maths, width often goes with length. A rectangle has a length and a width, and a rectangle's width is its shorter side in many shapes, so check the labels.
explain: Width can be small. «A helmet should sit about two fingers' width above the eyebrows.» Here width measures a small gap across your forehead. Try it: hold two fingers side by side and you have a width.
fact: Width means how wide something is, the distance from one side to the other.
fact: Width is a noun: one width, two widths.
fact: In maths, «the length is twice the width» tells you how a rectangle's two measurements compare.
fact: «A lock 20 metres long and 2 metres wide» shows that length and width are both measured in metres.
fact: «Mars is about half the Earth's width.» This compares how wide the two planets are.
exercise: «A lock 20 metres long and 2 metres wide.» What is the width of the lock? | 40 metres | 3 metres | *2 metres | 20 metres
exercise: Which word measures the distance from one side of something to the other? | *Width | Weight | Length | Time
exercise: «A helmet should sit about two fingers' width above the eyebrows.» What does width measure here? | The colour of the strap | The number of fingers | The weight of the helmet | *A small distance across, like two fingers side by side
test: A rectangle is 8 cm long and 5 cm wide. What is its width? | *5 cm | 8 cm | 13 cm | 40 cm
test: «Mars is about half the Earth's width.» What is being compared? | How tall the two planets are | How fast the planets spin | How far the planets are from the Sun | *How wide the two planets are
exam: Which word means the distance from one side of something to the other? | *Width | Depth | Weight | Height
